From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:10:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zink: no triangle fans on KosmicKrisp

Metal has no triangle fans. KosmicKrisp draws one by unrolling it into
a triangle list in a compute pass before the draw, and on Metal a
compute pass ends the render pass: the colour and depth attachments are
stored and loaded again around every fan draw. Zink also draws quads
through a geometry shader when the device has fans, which KosmicKrisp
runs as compute too.

With the screen reporting no triangle fans, the gallium frontend turns
fans and quads into triangle lists on the CPU, as it does on drivers
whose portability subset has no fans.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-zink-followups.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
index 9340695..7552f08 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -3709,6 +3709,13 @@ zink_internal_create_screen(const struct pipe_screen_config *config, int64_t dev
       screen->have_triangle_fans = (VK_TRUE == screen->info.portability_subset_feats.triangleFans);
    }
 #endif // VK_KHR_PORTABILITY_SUBSET_EXTENSION_NAME
+   /* KosmicKrisp draws a triangle fan through a compute pass that unrolls
+    * it, which ends the Metal render pass at every fan draw: the gallium
+    * frontend converts fans (and quads, which would take a geometry shader)
+    * into triangle lists instead.
+    */
+   if (zink_driverid(screen) == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_KOSMICKRISP)
+      screen->have_triangle_fans = false;
 
    check_base_requirements(screen);
    util_live_shader_cache_init(&screen->shaders, zink_create_gfx_shader_state, zink_delete_shader_state);
-- 
